{"name":"Fresh Roe","hex":"#503e2c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fresh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Newly produced or obtained; recent.","(of food) Not dried, frozen, or spoiled."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Recently; just recently; most recently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fresh"},{"term":"roe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ronji."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Eggs of fish.","Sperm of certain fish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roe","blocks":[{"text":"Roe, or hard roe, is the fully ripe internal egg masses in the ovaries, or the released external egg masses, of fish and certain marine animals such as shrimp, scallop, sea urchins and squid. As a seafood, roe is used both as a cooked ingredient in many dishes, and as a raw ingredient for delicacies such as caviar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Caviar_spoons.jpg/330px-Caviar_spoons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roe","wikidata":"Q219426"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Prawns_Skagen_with_cold-smoked_salmon_roe_on_bread.jpg/500px-Prawns_Skagen_with_cold-smoked_salmon_roe_on_bread.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Prawns_Skagen_with_cold-smoked_salmon_roe_on_bread.jpg/1280px-Prawns_Skagen_with_cold-smoked_salmon_roe_on_bread.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Prawns_Skagen_with_cold-smoked_salmon_roe_on_bread.jpg/500px-Prawns_Skagen_with_cold-smoked_salmon_roe_on_bread.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Swedish toast Skagen toppe